From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:42:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Image size: model dimensions win over the first texture

getSize() returned the first texture's real size whenever a texture was
bound, so a layer whose first texture is a mask was drawn at the mask size:
deep_space Background (flowimage: flowmask 480x270 + 1920x1080 layers) ended
up as a small rotated rectangle in the middle of the scene. The model's
width/height define the quad; fall back to the texture only without them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp b/src/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
index be0baca..ef509d4 100644
--- a/src/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
+++ b/src/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CImage.cpp
@@ -1133,6 +1133,11 @@ glm::vec2 CImage::getSize () const {
     if (this->m_texture == nullptr) {
 	return this->getImage ().size;
     }
+    // The model's dimensions define the quad: the first texture can be a mask
+    // (e.g. a 480x270 flowmask over 1920x1080 layers) rather than the image itself.
+    if (this->getImage ().model->width.has_value () && this->getImage ().model->height.has_value ()) {
+	return { this->getImage ().model->width.value (), this->getImage ().model->height.value () };
+    }
 
     return { this->m_texture->getRealWidth (), this->m_texture->getRealHeight () };
 }
